### Constraint Note
The draft was at 4,487 words against a hard 4,500 lint ceiling, so the bridges had to be paid for. The cuts above are all genuine redundancy, not compression of unique content. Final: **4,493 words, blog-lint 0 fail**, same 3 pre-existing warns (no `faqs` frontmatter, 1 comparative contrast pattern, thin word headroom).

### Remaining Concern
Section 8 now carries two arguments in sequence — repetition-as-trust-inventory, then Emma Frost refuting it. That unresolved tension is deliberate per the ledger and I left it intact, but it means the section's own through-line ends on a question rather than a claim. If a later pass ever wants a cleaner landing, splitting Emma Frost into its own short section is the move. Your call.
